{"total_count":7,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/11340","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/11340/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/11340/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/11340/events","html_url":"https://github.com/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/11340","id":849860054,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU4NDk4NjAwNTQ=","number":11340,"title":"Allow filtering by \"Open Now\" in map profile POI overlay settings and on map","user":{"login":"xeruf","id":13354331,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMzU0MzMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13354331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xeruf","html_url":"https://github.com/xeruf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xeruf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xeruf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xeruf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xeruf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xeruf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xeruf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xeruf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xeruf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xeruf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":204955796,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDQ5NTU3OTY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/labels/Nice%20to%20Have","name":"Nice to Have","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":"Should be fixed but there is no priority or no possibility to fix it within current horizon planning","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2021-04-04T11:59:26Z","updated_at":"2021-04-07T18:25:04Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!--🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅\r\n\r\nOh hi there! 😄\r\n\r\nTo expedite issue processing please search open and closed issues before submitting a new one.\r\nExisting issues often contain information about workarounds, resolution, or progress updates.\r\n\r\nGitHub is our main development tool for our developers. There are hundreds of requests a month and there are relatively few developers.\r\nSo by opening an issue, please know that your issue will be sent out to all developers and acknowledge that it could be closed without explanation or with just a brief message.\r\nComments on the closed issues are also sent to all developers, so you definitely will be heard.\r\nHowever, there is no guarantee that a developer will pick up the issue to work on it.\r\n\r\nPlease be sure to read our [FAQ](https://osmand.net/help-online) before creating an issue here.\r\n\r\n🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅🔅-->\r\n\r\n# 🚀 feature request\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nSearching for an open POI, especially on holidays, can be tiresome, since the map quickly gets crowded. Yes I can go into the filter settings and add the filter there, but that takes too many clicks, especially since I would prefer only seeing open ones by default.\r\n\r\n### Describe the solution you'd like\r\n\r\nIn the default POI overlay for a map profile I'd like to be able to only show non-closed POIs. I know I can create new filters, but since I have multiple map profiles that each use multiple selections, this can quickly become annoying.\r\n\r\n### Describe alternatives you've considered\r\n\r\nAlternatively, a toggle directly on the map view to only display open POIs could be handy.\r\n\r\nRelated to  #3350","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/11340/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/11340/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/25734","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/25734/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/25734/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/25734/events","html_url":"https://github.com/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/25734","id":5237588055,"node_id":"I_kwDOABM0Ss8AAAABOC9AVw","number":25734,"title":"Cycling Profile: Never route over A-roads, allow B-roads","user":{"login":"secretmango","id":78762110,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NzYyMTEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78762110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/secretmango","html_url":"https://github.com/secretmango","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secretmango/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secretmango/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secretmango/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secretmango/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secretmango/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secretmango/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secretmango/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secretmango/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secretmango/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":204955796,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDQ5NTU3OTY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/labels/Nice%20to%20Have","name":"Nice to Have","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":"Should be fixed but there is no priority or no possibility to fix it within current horizon planning","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-08-24T17:28:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T21:00:04Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This is an important issue.\n\nIn many rural regions like Sweden and I suppose also Germany, there are no real bicycle byways, so you will be routed along \"B-roads / country roads / Landstraße / landsväg\". This is fine as they are generally less crowded and don't have a middle strip dividing the street.\n\nIn sweden at least there were also \"A-roads / Bundesstraßen / ...\" which have a strip dividing the street, are more crowded and sometimes even have guardrails on the side.\n\nThose streets are extremely dangerous and cyclists are generally not expected there. They are displayed in orange rather than yellow (as far as I remember) so OSMAnd knows the difference.\n\nPlease adapt the cycling profile(s) to NEVER route along these orange roads.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/25734/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/25734/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/22978","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/22978/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/22978/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/22978/events","html_url":"https://github.com/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/22978","id":3221006743,"node_id":"I_kwDOABM0Ss6__KmX","number":22978,"title":"Add setting to hide or show residential rooftop solar panels","user":{"login":"stragu","id":1747497,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDc0OTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1747497?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stragu","html_url":"https://github.com/stragu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stragu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stragu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stragu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stragu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stragu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stragu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stragu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stragu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stragu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":204955796,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDQ5NTU3OTY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/labels/Nice%20to%20Have","name":"Nice to Have","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":"Should be fixed but there is no priority or no possibility to fix it within current horizon planning","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-07-10T23:47:44Z","updated_at":"2025-08-05T22:16:45Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the idea\n\nIt would be great to have a setting to hide rooftop solar systems specifically, because they make the map very crowded in some areas.\n\nSee these two screenshots, at two different zoom levels:\n\n<img width=\"350\"  alt=\"screenshot at higher zoom level, the icon is a single thunderbolt\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/256edcc3-5982-4271-b3a6-c1d4a45f1a7a\" />\n\n<img width=\"350\" alt=\"screenshot at lower zoom level, the icon is a combination of a solar panel + a sun + a thunderbolt\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/80ea822d-0986-410f-94c5-349e31070190\" />\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nEither:\n\n* have a setting to hide specifically rooftop solar panels (without hiding non-rooftop, larger-scale solar power plants); or\n* hide them by default but add a setting in \"Details\" to turn them on\n\nThe corresponding preset from iD is called \"Rooftop Solar Panel\" in English and currently uses the following tags:\n\n```\ngenerator:method=photovoltaic\ngenerator:output:electricity=yes\ngenerator:source=solar\ngenerator:type=solar_photovoltaic_panel\nlocation=roof\npower=generator\n```\n\nMy guess is that the criteria to differentiate between residential rooftop vs large-scale power plants would be both the `location=roof` tag as well as an area threshold if tagged as a (multi)polygon.\n\n### Alternatives you've considered\n\nCurrently, the only way to hide them I know of is by using Map Rendering > Hide > Overground objects, but that hides pretty much everything visible on the ground.\n\n### Context\n\nThe version I currently use: OsmAnd~ 5.1.3 from F-Droid; paid account for live updates.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/22978/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/22978/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/15166","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/15166/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/15166/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/15166/events","html_url":"https://github.com/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/15166","id":1353036995,"node_id":"I_kwDOABM0Ss5QpbTD","number":15166,"title":"OpenGL: With OSM-carto, Park operators are too intrusive","user":{"login":"michaelblyons","id":2701605,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDE2MDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2701605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelblyons","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelblyons","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelblyons/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelblyons/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelblyons/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelblyons/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelblyons/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelblyons/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelblyons/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelblyons/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelblyons/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2022-08-27T12:47:32Z","updated_at":"2022-08-29T12:32:17Z","closed_at":"2022-08-29T12:32:17Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description\r\n\r\nThe OpenGL version is newly available to me. (Thanks F-Droid maintainers!) It looks great. It loads fast.\r\n\r\nBut my primary map style is [OSM-carto][1] which on OGL (but not before?) shows the `operator` tag for parks. Since my local area has a number of parks, the viewing area is really crowded with text for them.\r\n\r\n### How to reproduce?\r\n\r\n- Change map style to OSM-carto.\r\n- Find (or add tags to!) a nearby park to add its operator.\r\n- See lots of text and irregular line spacing.\r\n\r\n### Your Environment\r\n\r\nOsmAnd Version: OsmAnd~ 4.2.7\r\nAndroid/iOS version: 12\r\nDevice model: Pixel\r\n\r\n[1]: https://github.com/osmandapp/OsmAnd-resources/blob/master/rendering_styles/osm-carto.render.xml\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/15166/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/15166/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/40","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/40/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/40/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/osmandapp/OsmAnd/issues/40/events","html_url":"https://github.com/osmandapp/OsmAnd/pull/40","id":1479026,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0Mjg5Mjk0","number":40,"title":"removed 'items' im Offline Data Manager to make list less crowded.","user":{"login":"sonora","id":8